In Terraform, locals are used to define local variables inside a Terraform configuration.
They help you avoid repeating the same values multiple times and make the code clean and reusable.

Think of locals like temporary variables used only inside the Terraform project.

1. Simple Definition (Beginner Friendly)
locals = a place where you define calculated or reusable values.

You define them once and reuse them many times.

Example syntax:

locals {
  variable_name = value
}
Then use it like this:

local.variable_name
2. Why DevOps Engineers Use locals
In real DevOps projects we often need:

Standard naming for resources

Environment names (dev / qa / prod)

Tags

Common values used across multiple resources

Instead of repeating them everywhere, we define them in locals.

Benefits:

✔ Cleaner Terraform code
✔ Avoid repetition
✔ Easier to maintain
✔ Easier environment management

3. Real AWS Example (EC2 + Standard Naming)
Imagine you are creating an EC2 instance in AWS and want a standard naming convention.

Example naming rule:

company-env-appname
Example:

mycompany-prod-web
Terraform Example
Step 1 — Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
}
Step 2 — Define Locals
locals {

  company = "mycompany"
  environment = "prod"
  application = "web"

  instance_name = "${local.company}-${local.environment}-${local.application}"

}
Here we created:

instance_name = mycompany-prod-web
Step 3 — Use Local Variable
resource "aws_instance" "web" {

  ami           = "ami-0f58b397bc5c1f2e8"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = local.instance_name
  }

}
Now the EC2 instance name will be:

mycompany-prod-web
4. Real DevOps Example (Common Tags)
In real companies we add standard tags to every AWS resource.

Example:

Environment

Owner

Project

Terraform

Instead of repeating them everywhere, we use locals.

locals.tf
locals {

  common_tags = {
    Environment = "prod"
    Owner       = "devops-team"
    Project     = "payment-service"
    ManagedBy   = "Terraform"
  }

}
Use in Resources
resource "aws_instance" "app" {

  ami           = "ami-0f58b397bc5c1f2e8"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"

  tags = local.common_tags
}
Now every resource automatically gets standard tags.

This is very common in production Terraform projects.

5. Locals with Calculations
Locals can also calculate values.

Example:

locals {

  instance_count = 3

  instance_names = [
    "web-1",
    "web-2",
    "web-3"
  ]

}
6. Locals vs Variables (Important for Interviews)
Feature	Locals	Variables
Purpose	Internal reusable values	Input from user
Scope	Only inside Terraform code	Passed from outside
Defined	locals {}	variable {}
Usage	local.name	var.name
Example:

var.environment   -> user input
local.name_prefix -> calculated internally
